# GenTRX environment template
# copy to .env and fill in values.
# .env is gitignored; .env.example is the committed template.
#
# Sourced automatically by:
#   - run_validator.sh (production)
#   - agents/proxy/run (proxy test)

# ============================================================
# Local development paths
# ============================================================

# Path to the active venv (used by proxy/localnet test launchers).
# If you have a venv activated when running the launcher, this can be empty.
TAOS_VENV=/path/to/venv

# Path to the proxy directory (relative to repo root, used by proxy test).
TAOS_PROXY=agents/proxy

# Path to taosim build directory.
TAOS_BUILD=simulate/trading/build

# ============================================================
# Local MinIO (default for localnet/proxy testing)
# ============================================================
# Container name is always "gentrx_minio". Same MinIO instance hosts all
# GenTRX buckets in localnet (validator bucket + per-miner gradient buckets).
# Change credentials before any non-local deployment.

GENTRX_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin
GENTRX_SECRET_KEY=minioadmin

# MinIO ports: only override if the defaults are taken.
# Note on the console port: default is 9091 (not MinIO's own 9001) because
# bittensor's --prometheus.port defaults to 9001. Keeping MinIO's console on
# 9091 prevents the validator's Prometheus server from EADDRINUSE'ing on startup.
# MINIO_PORT=9000
# MINIO_CONSOLE=9091

# Chain endpoint override, used by miner-bucket discovery via the
# Commitments pallet. On-chain commitments only carry account_id; for
# self-hosted MinIO we override to the public endpoint of this MinIO.
# LEAVE COMMENTED OUT for R2/Hippius. URLs derive from account_id.
# The localnet test's setup_minio exports this to http://localhost:9000
# automatically at runtime, so you do NOT need to set it in .env for
# localnet either.
# GENTRX_CHAIN_ENDPOINT_OVERRIDE=http://localhost:9000

# ============================================================
# Production S3 (R2 / Hippius)
# ============================================================
# Single validator bucket per validator: checkpoints/ + data/ + scores/.
# Read credentials are committed to chain at startup.
# Miners and the aggregator discover the bucket without pre-configuration.
# Supported providers: Cloudflare R2 and Hippius S3.
#
# Cloudflare R2:
#   ACCOUNT_ID is the 32-char hex Cloudflare account ID (appears in R2 dashboard).
#   Endpoint is derived automatically: https://{account_id}.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
#   Create a new R2 account (or sub-account) per validator bucket.
#
# Hippius S3:
#   Omit ACCOUNT_ID, BUCKET is stored in the account_id field on-chain.
#   Endpoint is https://s3.hippius.com, region is decentralized (auto-detected).
#
# WARNING: agents/proxy/setup_minio does `export` (unconditional) on
# every GENTRX_VALIDATOR_S3_* below when it runs.  Do NOT invoke setup_minio
# for R2/Hippius deployments.

# --- Validator's own bucket (set on every validator host) ---
# Writeable. Holds checkpoints, data parquets, and aggregation proposals.
# Miners do NOT set these.
# GENTRX_VALIDATOR_S3_BUCKET=<bucket-name>
# GENTRX_VALIDATOR_S3_ACCOUNT_ID=<R2-account-id>        # R2 only; omit for Hippius
# GENTRX_VALIDATOR_S3_READ_ACCESS_KEY=<read-only-key>   # committed to chain
# GENTRX_VALIDATOR_S3_READ_SECRET_KEY=<read-only-secret>
# GENTRX_VALIDATOR_S3_WRITE_ACCESS_KEY=<write-key>      # never leaves this host
# GENTRX_VALIDATOR_S3_WRITE_SECRET_KEY=<write-secret>

# --- Aggregator (uid-0) bucket fallback ---
# Read-only. Used by miners (always) and sibling validators (optional) as
# the chain-discovery fallback for the canonical checkpoint source. Uid-0
# publishes these in the subnet README/Discord; pin them here. The
# aggregator itself does NOT set these.
# GENTRX_AGGREGATOR_S3_BUCKET=<uid-0-bucket>
# GENTRX_AGGREGATOR_S3_ENDPOINT_URL=https://<account_id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# GENTRX_AGGREGATOR_S3_ACCOUNT_ID=<uid-0-R2-account-id>   # R2 only; omit for Hippius
# GENTRX_AGGREGATOR_S3_READ_ACCESS_KEY=<published-read-key>
# GENTRX_AGGREGATOR_S3_READ_SECRET_KEY=<published-read-secret>

# --- Per-miner bucket: gradient uploads (each miner has their own) ---
# Set these per-miner. Read creds are committed on-chain at miner startup.
# GENTRX_AGENT_S3_BUCKET=<miner-bucket>
# GENTRX_AGENT_S3_ENDPOINT_URL=https://<account>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# GENTRX_AGENT_S3_ACCESS_KEY=<miner-write-key>
# GENTRX_AGENT_S3_SECRET_KEY=<miner-write-secret>
# Read-only creds for chain commitment (separate from write creds in production):
# GENTRX_AGENT_S3_READ_ACCESS_KEY=<read-only-key>
# GENTRX_AGENT_S3_READ_SECRET_KEY=<read-only-secret>
# GENTRX_AGENT_S3_ACCOUNT_ID=<R2-account-id>  # optional, for R2; defaults to bucket name

# ============================================================
# Validator ↔ gradient server auth (cross-machine setups only)
# ============================================================
# Shared secret. NOT needed when both processes run on the same host (the
# gradient server binds 127.0.0.1 by default. Loopback is closed to the
# network). Required on cross-machine setups where the gradient server binds
# to a non-loopback interface; set the same value on both hosts. Generate
# with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
#
# See doc/gentrx/validator_setup.md "Connecting the validator to the
# gradient server" for full setup (curl verification, firewall notes, TLS).
# GENTRX_API_KEY=<long-random-string>

# ============================================================
# run_validator.sh: validator/simulator settings
# ============================================================
# Defaults are set inside run_validator.sh. Override here for non-mainnet
# or non-default wallet/hotkey setups. No Docker required for the base
# validator+simulator stack: the simulator is a pre-built C++ binary.
#
# Example: localnet / devnet (chain not on finney)
# ENDPOINT=ws://<localnet-ip>:9945
# NETUID=<local-netuid>
# WALLET_PATH=/path/to/wallets
# WALLET_NAME=<wallet-name>
# HOTKEY_NAME=validator
# SIMULATION_CONFIG=simulation_0   # XML config name under simulate/trading/run/config/
# PRESERVE_SIMULATOR=1             # skip rebuild; use the existing taosim binary
# USE_TMUX=0                       # disable tmux (useful in headless CI/pm2 setups)
# VALIDATOR_UID=<your-uid>         # used in GenTRX Prometheus labels; find with:
#                                  #   btcli wallet overview --netuid $NETUID

# ============================================================
# Production validator: GenTRX opt-in (run_validator.sh)
# ============================================================
# run_validator.sh passes this through to validator.py verbatim. Leave unset
# to run the validator without GenTRX. To enable, uncomment and point at your
# gradient server (loopback for single-host, external endpoint for multi-host):
#
# GENTRX_VAL_ARGS="--gentrx.enabled --gentrx.gradient_server_url http://127.0.0.1:8100/gentrx --gentrx.api_key $GENTRX_API_KEY"
#
# The localnet test does NOT use this; its launcher wires GenTRX args directly.

# ============================================================
# Wandb dashboard (optional, gradient-server side only)
# ============================================================
# Live dashboard at wandb.ai. Miners don't need any of this.
# See doc/gentrx/wandb.md for full setup + privacy notes.
# WANDB_API_KEY=<your-key>                # or keep it in ~/.netrc
# WANDB_PROJECT=gentrx-<env>              # required to enable (e.g. gentrx-mainnet)
# WANDB_RUN_NAME=<optional-run-label>     # defaults to wandb auto-generated
# WANDB_MODE=offline                      # for air-gapped hosts; sync later
# WANDB_VERBOSE=true                      # adds per-miner detail panels
